# [DD-13b.W1.1 r46sem finding 14] `description | ` -- the block-scalar
# marker PLUS a trailing space. Ruled: compare the TRIMMED value in all
# three, so this is refused exactly like bare `description |`. Legs A
# and B used to accept it as the literal text "| " (an exact strcmp/
# string-compare that the trailing space slipped past); leg C already
# refused it (`v.strip() == '|'`), which was the one place leg C was
# STRICTER than its siblings rather than in step with them.
#
# [DD-13b.W23.1] THE VERDICT IS UNCHANGED AND THE REASON MOVED. The block
# `|` form is legal now (§1.2.5), so leg A no longer refuses this for being
# a head-only spelling — it refuses because the region it opens is EMPTY,
# the next line being at the opener's own indent. All three legs still
# refuse, which is what the fixture is for; the TRIM rule it pins (a `|`
# with trailing whitespace is nobody's intended literal) is untouched.
pattern a+
description | 
m "aaa" 0 3
